Hannah Li: Opening a small PR to the troubleshooting err-ref focused on 429 vs timeout handling + observability knobs. Want a tiny Go snippet showing Retry-After handling + fallback, a 2-line migration note, and one link fix. @Marco @Rhea please review.

Marco Silva: Nice. Go snippet would be useful (we don't have many Go examples). Keep it short and idiomatic. Also call out 'context trim' term once.

Rhea Kapoor: Also add a short line about emitting an error metric tag (error_type=429/timeout) so customers can alert. That helps SREs tune fallback policies.

Hannah Li: Draft Go snippet: 

```go
// minimal retry + fallback example
func GenerateWithFallback(client *redwood.Client, prompt string) (*redwood.Response, error) {
  resp, err := client.Text.Generate(ctx, redwood.GenerateParams{Model: "redwood-1", Prompt: prompt})
  if err != nil {
    if apiErr, ok := err.(redwood.APIError); ok && apiErr.Status == 429 {
      wait := apiErr.Headers.Get("Retry-After")
      d := time.Second
      if secs, e := strconv.Atoi(wait); e == nil { d = time.Duration(secs) * time.Second }
      time.Sleep(d)
      return client.Text.Generate(ctx, redwood.GenerateParams{Model: "redwood-1-small", Prompt: prompt})
    }
    if errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded) { // timeout
      return client.Text.Generate(ctx, redwood.GenerateParams{Model: "redwood-1-small", Prompt: prompt})
    }
    return nil, err
  }
  return resp, nil
}
```

Marco Silva: Good. Trim comments and shorten variable names where possible for doc rendering. Add a one-line snippet showing emitting a metric: `metrics.Incr("inference.error", 1, map[string]string{"error_type":"429"})`.

Rhea Kapoor: Migration blurb (short): "Quick migration: honor Retry-After headers, prefer backoff, and emit distinct metrics for 429 vs timeouts. Normalize wording to 'context trim' in docs to match runtime. Run small canaries before wide rollouts."

